---
description: Break work into phases; UT + mini-review each step; never batch large diffs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Phased delivery

## When starting non-trivial work

1. Split into phases (e.g. data/API wiring → UI → edge cases → docs). Prefer phases that each leave the tree green.
2. Share the phase list with the user when useful; adjust if they reorder/cut scope.

## Per phase (hard loop)

1. Implement only that phase’s files/behavior.
2. Add/update **unit tests for that phase** (happy + at least one negative/edge when relevant) — colocated `*.test.tsx` / `*.test.ts`.
3. Run **focused tests** for the touched area, then the **full suite** (`npm test`) before calling the phase done.
4. **Mini-review** the phase diff (correctness, readability, secrets) — present a short summary; do not start the next phase until this phase is verified.
5. Optionally commit the phase alone (easier bisect/review) when the user wants commits.

## Forbidden

- Implementing everything, then one giant test run and one giant review at the end.
